      "description": "Objective\nValidate which MuleSoft API endpoints are available and functional for SFCC to consume product, category, pricing, customer, order data — and document what is missing, broken, or requires updates before build can begin.\nBackground\nBefore the MuleSoft Product Integration story (SFCC-33) and Base Pricebook Setup (SFCC-35) can be built against live APIs, we need to understand the current state of the endpoints and agree what changes are required.\nTasks\nInventory all MuleSoft API endpoints relevant to SFCC: product feed, category/taxonomy, pricing/pricebook, and inventory\nFor each endpoint, assess: does it exist? Is it reachable in a non-prod environment? Does the response format match what SFCC expects?\nIdentify endpoints that are missing, returning incorrect data, or requiring transformation before SFCC can consume them\nDocument required changes and flag as MuleSoft-side (Zimmermann dependency) vs SFCC-side\nAgree on STUB data for any endpoints not yet ready, to unblock SFCC build\nDefinition of Done\nA documented endpoint map is produced covering status (available / needs update / missing) for each in-scope API, with clear ownership of required changes and an agreed timeline for resolution.",
