      "summary": "User Management & Reporting",
      "description": "Epic Name:\n User Management & Reporting\nEpic Summary\nThis epic covers Business Manager access design for Zimmermann staff — role-based permissions, separation of duties, and session management. It also covers scheduled data export jobs and API access configuration for downstream reporting pipelines.\nBusiness Value / Objective\nEnsuring the right people have the right access in BM at go-live is critical for operational readiness. Scheduled exports and API access support Zimmermann's data and reporting pipelines post-launch.\nScope\nIn Scope:\nBM role configuration aligned to Zimmermann's operating model (roles to be confirmed with Zimmermann)\nAction-level permissions and separation of duties configuration\nSession timeout configuration\nScheduled export jobs for transactional data (orders, returns, customers, products, inventory) in CSV/XML\nAuthenticated API access configuration for orders, products, customers, and inventory\nOut of Scope:\nSSO via Azure AD/Entra ID — Zimmermann scope; Accenture configures BM to accept SSO only\nData pipeline build and warehouse schema alignment — Zimmermann scope\nRole design and separation of duties matrix sign-off — Zimmermann to confirm\nDependencies\nAzure Active Directory / Entra ID — Zimmermann-managed SSO identity provider\nAssumptions & Constraints\nNumber and definition of BM roles to be confirmed with Zimmermann ahead of configuration\nSSO setup on the Entra ID side is Zimmermann's responsibility",
