      "id": "17838",
      "key": "SFCC-12",
      "summary": "Checkout Flow & Delivery",
      "description": "Epic Name:\n Checkout Flow & Delivery\nEpic Summary\nThis epic covers the end-to-end checkout flow for guest and registered customers in the Zimmermann PWA Kit storefront. It includes checkout entry and authentication, order summary, delivery address and validation, delivery method selection, billing address, order review, and order confirmation. For international storefronts (EU international, HK, ME, US international), SFCC hands off to Global-e who owns the full checkout experience.\nBusiness Value / Objective\nCheckout is the final and most critical step in the customer journey. A smooth, localised checkout experience across all 8 storefronts minimises drop-off and ensures orders are placed correctly and routed to the right fulfilment system at go-live.\nScope\nIn Scope:\nFull checkout flow for domestic storefronts: AU, US domestic, UK, EU domestic\nGuest and registered customer checkout paths including Omneo profile matching at entry\nDelivery address entry and validation (Google API), including PO Box/Parcel Locker blocking\nDelivery method selection with Narvar EDD display; Toshi concierge (US/UK), Uber same-day (AU)\nPackaging choice across all storefronts\nCollect in Boutique delivery option (AU, UK, EU domestic)\nBilling address entry including optional VAT/tax ID fields for EU domestic and UK\nOrder confirmation page and confirmation email trigger via Narvar (domestic) / Global-e (international)\nGlobal-e redirect and handoff for EU international, HK, ME, US international\nOut of Scope:\nPayment capture and payment methods — covered in SFCC-13 (Payments)\nReturns initiation — covered in SFCC-14 (Returns & Refunds)\nOrder history in My Account — covered in SFCC-15 (Order Management)\nGlobal-e checkout experience — Global-e scope; SFCC owns the handoff only\nCarrier label automation (Shippit, Ordoro) — OMS-level, not invoked from SFCC\nOrder confirmation email templates — Narvar/Zimmermann scope\nDependencies\nGoogle API — delivery and billing address autocomplete and validation\nNarvar — EDD display at delivery method selection; order confirmation email for domestic orders\nGlobal-e cartridge — international checkout handoff (EU international, HK, ME, US international)\nAvalara cartridge — tax calculation for US domestic, NZ, New Caledonia, EU domestic\nMuleSoft/NewStore OMS — order creation and delivery method routing at order placement\nOmneo — customer identity, saved addresses, and new account creation at checkout\nContentful — CMS-managed content within checkout (trust messaging, disclaimer text)\nAdyen cartridge — payment authorisation handoff including Klarna (AU and US)\nAssumptions & Constraints\nGlobal-e owns the full checkout experience for EU international, HK, ME and US international; SFCC owns the handoff only\nAU storefront processes all Oceania orders (including NZ and Pacific Islands) within SFCC — no Global-e handoff\nOmneo is the master for customer address data; addresses synced bidirectionally via MuleSoft\nIf Google API is unavailable, manual address entry is available as a fallback with no hard block on checkout progression\nNo order splits — all items in a single order must be delivered to the same address\nSocial login is not in scope; authentication is standard email and password only",
