      "key": "SFCC-41",
      "summary": "Promotion Stacking & Priority Rules",
      "description": "As a \nSite Merchandiser, \n\n\nI want\n to configure promotion stacking and priority rules in SFCC Business Manager, \n\n\nso that \nwhen multiple promotions are active simultaneously the correct discount behaviour is applied consistently.\nStacking rules by promotion type:\nProduct, order, and shipping promotions are stackable with each other — a customer can benefit from one of each type simultaneously. \nWithin the same promotion type, only the highest discount applies — discounts of the same type do not stack.\nPriority rules:\nPromotions can be assigned a priority in BM to determine which applies when exclusion rules are in play.\n\n\nCustomer group discount exclusion rules (sale items, gift cards) are configured in BM as part of each promotion's eligibility criteria — covered in the Customer Group Pricing & Discounts story.",
