    "content": {
      "value": "This page consolidates all open questions for the MuleSoft team relevant to the Zimmermann SFCC / PWA integration design. Where an answer is already known from existing documentation, it is pre-filled and flagged for **confirmation only**. Questions that are not MuleSoft's responsibility have been removed.\n\nCovers both **data sync (inbound to SFCC)** and **real-time API calls (SFCC/PWA → MuleSoft)**.\n\n**Legend:** - ✅ **Known** — answer pre-filled from existing documentation; MuleSoft to confirm - ❓ **Unknown** — no answer exists in any page; MuleSoft to answer\n\n> **Context for Sections 2, 3, and 4:** The SFCC integration for product, price, and inventory has not been built yet. MuleSoft's current integration experience is with Magento. These questions focus on understanding the current Magento process so the SFCC team can determine the right integration approach for each domain.\n\n---\n\n1-general--architecture1. General / Architecture\n------------------------------------------------\n\n| # | Domain | Question | What we need | Priority | Response |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| G1 | Architecture | Confirm MuleSoft API base URL pattern per environment. | ✅ Known: Dev → `https://mw.staging.zimmermann.com/{api-name}-dev/api/`, QA → `{api-name}-qa/api/`, Prod → `https://mw.staging.zimmermann.com/{api-name}/api/`. Confirm: is the production base domain `mw.zimmermann.com` (not `mw.staging.zimmermann.com`) and is UAT a separate environment with its own pattern? | P0 | * Dev and QA - correct * Prod - `https://mw.zimmermann.com/{api-name}/api/` * UAT is done in the staging environment |\n| G2 | Auth | Confirm auth mechanism for SFCC → MuleSoft real-time API calls. | ✅ Known: client credentials (client\\_id / client\\_secret) via Mule secure property placeholder. Confirm: are credentials issued per-environment (separate Dev / QA / Prod sets)? | P0 | * Yes - environment specific * Oauth tokens exist for experience apis |\n| G3 | Performance | What is the MuleSoft rate limit per API per environment? | ❓ The SFCC PWA spikes heavily on product launches and sales — Find In Store, order history, and checkout all make real-time MuleSoft calls. SFCC needs to know the limit to design client-side back-off or caching. | P0 | * Will source information * This specific API has a larger limit set for resource usage nevertheless |\n| G6 | Architecture | The SFCC team has access to Anypoint Exchange but the volume of specs makes it hard to identify which are relevant. | ❓ Please provide the specific Anypoint Exchange API spec names (or direct links) for the following touchpoints: customer outbound sync, order creation, order history & returns, and Find In Store. | P0 | * All Adobe endpoints to send data downstream will be within the Magento Experience API * Inv sync prc api and magento sys api for stock data into Adobe * Orders prc api for orders into Newstore |\n\n---\n\n2-product-sync-ap21--mulesoft--sfcc2. Product Sync (AP21 → MuleSoft → SFCC)\n---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n| # | Domain | Question | What we need | Priority | Response |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| P-M1a | Product Sync | What format does AP21 output for the product feed — XML, JSON, CSV, or another format? | ❓ Tells us whether MuleSoft already has an AP21 product connector reusable for SFCC. | P0 | * XML |\n| P-M1b | Product Sync | How is the AP21 product feed delivered to Magento — SFTP drop, API call, direct DB write, or another method? | ❓ | P0 | * Magento pulls data straight from Ap21 retail APIs * No Mulesoft involvement * Scheduled cron jobs in magento |\n| P-M1c | Product Sync | Does MuleSoft sit in the AP21 → Magento product path today, or is it a direct integration? | ❓ | P0 | * No Mulesoft involvement to send product data to Magento |\n| P-M2a | Product Sync | Does AP21 send the full product catalogue each run, or only products changed since the last export? | ❓ Volume and change detection capability are key inputs to the SFCC integration approach. | P0 | * Initial full import followed by deltas |\n| P-M2b | Product Sync | If delta — what is the change signal AP21 uses (last-modified timestamp, event, flag)? | ❓ | P0 |  |\n| P-M2c | Product Sync | What is the approximate catalogue volume — number of master styles and total variant SKUs in the current export? | ❓ | P0 |  |\n| P-M3a | Product Sync | Is the AP21 → Magento product feed triggered on a schedule, on AP21 product publish/update event, or both? If scheduled — what is the interval? | ❓ Sets the expected freshness SLA for SFCC. | P0 | * scheduler based (cron job) |\n| P-M3b | Product Sync | How quickly does a product change in AP21 become live on Magento today — minutes, hours, or overnight? | ❓ | P0 |  |\n| P-M4 | Product Sync | When a product is archived or suppressed in AP21, how does Magento know to take it offline — does AP21 send an explicit status flag, or is the product simply absent from the next feed? | ❓ SFCC merge mode will keep a product live indefinitely if it is merely absent — an explicit offline signal is required. | P0 | * Done inmagento natively |\n| P-M5a | Product Sync | Does MuleSoft transform the AP21 product payload before Magento receives it, or does Magento consume the raw AP21 format directly? | ❓ For SFCC, MuleSoft will need to produce a new output format — understanding re-use potential of the current mapping. | P0 | * Raw ap21 xml |\n| P-M5b | Product Sync | If MuleSoft transforms — where is the field mapping defined (MuleSoft DataWeave, a config file, or a mapping table)? | ❓ | P0 |  |\n| P-M6 | Error Handling | Does the MuleSoft failure alert for the product feed include individual failed product IDs, or only a job-level notification? | ✅ Known: 3 retries, automated email alert on failure. Confirm: per-product IDs or job-level only? | P1 |  |\n\n---\n\n3-price-sync-ap21--mulesoft--sfcc3. Price Sync (AP21 → MuleSoft → SFCC)\n-----------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n| # | Domain | Question | What we need | Priority | Response |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| PR-M1a | Price Sync | Does AP21 send price data bundled with the product export, or as a separate price-only feed? | ❓ Determines whether MuleSoft owns price sync for SFCC or whether it needs to be scoped as new work. | P0 | * Separate price feed to Magento straight from ap21 |\n| PR-M1b | Price Sync | Does MuleSoft currently process or transform AP21 price data before Magento receives it, or is it a direct AP21 → Magento connection? | ❓ | P0 | * Direct ap21 → Magento connection |\n| PR-M2a | Price Sync | Are price updates sent on the same schedule as product updates, or does AP21 emit a separate price change event? | ❓ Informs whether SFCC pricebook import needs a frequent schedule or a seasonal trigger. | P1 | * Separate cron job and data import for prices. * Magento runs the scheduled job and hits the Ap21 retail endpoints to fetch updated price data |\n| PR-M2b | Price Sync | Approximately how often do prices change in AP21 — daily, weekly, or on seasonal sale events only? | ❓ | P1 |  |\n| PR-M3a | Price Sync | Does AP21 have a dedicated `special_price` field, a date-ranged sale flag, or a separate sale price record per product? | ❓ Critical for SFCC: sale pricebook entries are not auto-removed — MuleSoft must send an explicit removal signal. | P0 |  |\n| PR-M3b | Price Sync | When a sale ends, does AP21 explicitly clear the sale price, or does it simply stop sending it? | ❓ | P0 | * Price is updated once sale ends |\n| PR-M3c | Price Sync | How does Magento currently handle sale price removal — does it rely on an explicit AP21 signal or does it expire sale prices by date? | ❓ | P0 | * Driven by the sync |\n\n---\n\n4-inventory-sync--mulesoft--sfcc4. Inventory Sync (→ MuleSoft → SFCC)\n---------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n> **Note:** The current MuleSoft `inventory-sync-prc-api` covers GB, AU, and US sourced from NewStore. The source system for **ZimmermannEU (domestic)**, **ZimmermannEUIntl**, **ZimmermannHK**, and **ZimmermannME** is unconfirmed — it may be AP21 directly, NewStore, or a shared regional pool. This must be established before any SFCC inventory design for those sites can proceed.\n\n| # | Domain | Question | What we need | Priority | Response |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| I-M1a | Inventory Sync | Does MuleSoft currently push inventory to Magento on the same 15-minute schedule as the NewStore sync, or is the Magento inventory update a different process? | ❓ Determines how much of the existing MuleSoft inventory flow can be reused for SFCC. | P0 | * 5 minute interval push from Newstore to Magento * Magento stores and pushes in intervals * Once pushed seen in storefront |\n| I-M1b | Inventory Sync | What format does Magento receive inventory in — API call per SKU, batch file, or direct DB update? | ❓ | P0 | * JSON format * Products and ATP sent |\n| I-M1c | Inventory Sync | Does MuleSoft sit in the Magento inventory path today, or does NewStore push to Magento directly? | ❓ | P0 | * Pushed through mulesoft flow |\n| I-M2 | Inventory Sync | Does the current Magento inventory update include per-location stock levels (DC + boutique), or is it an aggregated available quantity per SKU across all locations? | ❓ SFCC inventory lists store a single qty per SKU per list — if MuleSoft currently sends location-level detail, it will need to aggregate before writing to SFCC. | P0 | * Stock data sent with location info |\n| I-M3 | Inventory Sync | When a SKU goes OOS in NewStore, does MuleSoft send qty=0 to Magento, or is the record removed entirely from the inventory feed? | ❓ A missing inventory record in SFCC defaults to the `default-instock` setting on the inventory list — sending qty=0 explicitly is the safe approach. | P1 | * Needs to be checked |\n| I-M4a | Inventory Sync | For ZimmermannEU domestic — does NewStore manage EU fulfilment locations, or is EU stock held and managed in AP21 only? | ❓ Determines whether the existing `inventory-sync-prc-api` can be extended or whether a new AP21 → SFCC inventory flow is required for EU. | P0 | * For SFCC pov it will be newstore - cutover soon |\n| I-M4b | Inventory Sync | For ZimmermannEUIntl, ZimmermannHK, ZimmermannME — are these Global-e sites fulfilling from a shared EU or AU stock pool, or from dedicated regional locations? | ❓ | P0 |  |\n| I-M4c | Inventory Sync | Which system (NewStore or AP21) is the source of available inventory quantities for ZimmermannEU, ZimmermannEUIntl, ZimmermannHK, and ZimmermannME? | ❓ | P0 | * FOr non integrated ones , inventory pulled straight from AP21. Rest run on the Mulesoft sync |\n| I-M5 | Inventory Sync | Has MuleSoft updated `inventory-sync-prc-api` to target legacy SFCC inventory lists (`inventory_m_au`, `inventory_m_uk`, `inventory_m_us`) rather than OCI endpoints? | ✅ Known: Zimmermann uses legacy SFCC inventory lists, not OCI. The INT register (INT-013) incorrectly references SFCC OCI API. Confirm the update has been made. | P0 |  |\n| I-M6a | Inventory Sync | Does NewStore include a buffer stock level as a separate field in the inventory payload (e.g. `buffer_qty`, `safety_stock`, or similar), distinct from the raw on-hand quantity? | ❓ To correctly calculate online available stock for SFCC, we need to know whether NewStore provides buffer stock as an explicit field or whether it is embedded in the ATP quantity. If NewStore surfaces buffer separately, MuleSoft can subtract it from the on-hand quantity before writing to SFCC — ensuring the SFCC `allocation` value reflects true online-available stock rather than total physical stock. | P0 | * Currently done natively on Magento. |\n| I-M6b | Inventory Sync | If NewStore provides a buffer stock field — can MuleSoft calculate `online available stock = on-hand qty − buffer qty` and write the result as the `allocation` value in the SFCC invento