 |\n| OM-007 | Order Creation & Processing | The system will pass the selected delivery method to the OMS as a structured attribute; NewStore OMS maps this to the appropriate carrier and fulfilment route. | Accenture | ALL | Custom | Confirmed |  |\n| OM-008 | Fulfilment & Delivery | The system will display available delivery methods to the customer at checkout, sourced from configuration in SFCC Business Manager per storefront; available methods, display names, descriptions, and costs are configured per site. | Dependent SF Functionality | ALL | Config | Confirmed |  |\n| OM-009 | Fulfilment & Delivery | The system will display an estimated delivery timeframe alongside each delivery method (sourced from Narvar CONVERT widget for domestic storefronts, or Global-e for international). | Accenture | ALL | Custom | Confirmed |  |\n| OM-010 | Fulfilment & Delivery | ~~The system can apply free shipping thresholds per storefront as configured in Business Manager.~~ The system will support configurable free shipping thresholds in SFCC Business Manager, configurable independently per delivery method and per storefront. | Dependent SF Functionality | ALL | Config | Confirmed |  |\n| OM-011 | Fulfilment & Delivery | The system will pass the customer's selected delivery method to the OMS via MuleSoft; NewStore OMS owns all downstream carrier selection, dispatch, and label generation. | Accenture | ALL | Custom | Confirmed |  |\n| OM-012 | Fulfilment & Delivery | The system will allow the customer to select a boutique and proceed to payment; full payment is required at placement for BOPIS orders. | Accenture | UK (domestic), AU (domestic), EU (domestic), UK (domestic) | Custom | Confirmed |  |\n| OM-013 | Fulfilment & Delivery | The system will pass the selected boutique ID and a 'collect from boutique' flag to NewStore OMS via MuleSoft; NewStore OMS owns all BOPIS fulfilment logic from this point. | Accenture | UK (domestic), AU (domestic), EU (domestic), UK (domestic) | Custom | Confirmed |  |\n| OM-014 | Fulfilment & Delivery | The system will prevent Collect From Boutique selection for orders containing gift card products. | Accenture | UK (domestic), AU (domestic), EU (domestic), UK (domestic) | Custom | Confirmed |  |\n| OM-015 | Fulfilment & Delivery | The system will display BOPIS order status in My Account: Processing → Ready to Collect → Collected / Cancelled. | Zimmerman | UK (domestic), AU (domestic), EU (domestic), UK (domestic) | Custom | Confirmed |  |\n| OM-016 | Fulfilment & Delivery | The system will allow some products to be configurable as not available for fulfilment through Collect in Boutique (e.g. gift cards) | Accenture | UK (domestic), AU (domestic), EU (domestic), UK (domestic) | Config | Confirmed |  |\n| OM-017 | Fulfilment & Delivery | The system will display current order status in the Order page of My Account, sourced from NewStore OMS via MuleSoft at page load. | Accenture | ALL | Custom | Confirmed |  |\n| OM-018 | Fulfilment & Delivery | The system will display current order status ~~and shipment-level status only~~ on the Order Detail page of My Account, sourced from NewStore OMS via MuleSoft at page load. | Accenture | ALL | Custom | Confirmed |  |\n| OM-019 | Fulfilment & Delivery | The system will display a tracking link in My Account order detail for domestic orders this links to a Narvar tracking page; for international orders this is a Global-e tracking link. | Accenture | ALL | Custom | Confirmed |  |\n| OM-020 | Fulfilment & Delivery | ~~The system will be able to display order details page for scenarios, including split shipment, partial fulfilment information. 3PL tracking number is not shared.~~ The system will display order-level status on the order detail page as returned by NewStore via MuleSoft. Shipment-level detail, split shipment and partial fulfilment information are not displayed in SFCC - customers are directed to Narvar (domestic) or Global-e (international) for tracking. Internal 3PL tracking numbers will not be displayed to the customer. | Dependent SF Functionality | ALL | Custom | Confirmed |  |\n| OM-021 | Inventory | The system will consume a delta inventory feed on a set schedule, containing per size + colour stock level. This will come via MuleSoft | Accenture | ALL | Config | Confirmed |  |\n| OM-022 | Inventory | The system will consume a SFS inventory availability feed, which will be used to determine whether stock from that store should be used in total availability calculation for the SKU on the site | Accenture | ALL | Config | Confirmed |  |\n| OM-023 | Inventory | The system will consume a store opening hours feed daily (sourced from Google Business) for use in the boutique selector and store locator. | Accenture | ALL | Config | Confirmed |  |\n| OM-024 | Inventory | The system will be able to deduct a buffer stock value from storefront inventory calculation | Accenture | ALL | Custom | Confirmed |  |\n| OM-025 | Inventory | The system will allow a business user to configure the buffer stock value against a SKU, or a category. Any SKU-level buffer stock value will take precedence over category-level buffer-stock value. | Accenture | ALL | Config | Confirmed | @Jasmijn Tsang Confirm this with Mani, believe that we can only do SKU-level buffer stock. Category to be done via Excel (check enhancements)    This is not a standard configuration in BM. This buffer stock needs to be part of the inventory sync - either set in NewStore/AP21 or in MuleSoft if not in NewStore/AP21. Question to MuleSoft team |\n| OM-026 | Inventory | The system will allow a business user to bulk upload the buffer stock value against a list of categories | Accenture | ALL | Config | Confirmed |  |\n| OM-027 | Inventory | The system will allow a business user to bulk upload the buffer stock value against a list of SKUs, for the full set of SKUs per storefront | Accenture | ALL | Config | Confirmed |  |\n| OM-028 | Inventory | The system will allow a business user to trigger a bulk buffer stock update filtered by category, colour, and store view | Accenture | ALL | Config | Confirmed |  |\n| OM-029 | Inventory | The system will display per-size stock availability on PDP; out-of-stock sizes are visually indicated and cannot be added to bag. | Dependent SF Functionality | ALL | Custom | Confirmed |  |\n| OM-030 | Inventory | The system will incorporate buffer stock calculations in the availability display on the PDP | Accenture | ALL | Custom | Confirmed |  |\n| OM-031 | Inventory | The system will display a 'Find in Boutique' modal on PDP showing per-boutique availability for the selected product and size, using Google Maps and browser geolocation. | Accenture | ALL | Custom | Confirmed |  |\n| OM-032 | Inventory | The system will not apply buffer stock to availability calculation on the Find In Boutique overlay | Accenture | ALL | Custom | Confirmed |  |\n| OM-033 | Inventory | The system will be able to display a \"Notify me when back in stock\" button when a particular SKU is out of stock. Customer will be able to enter their email, have it be stored in SFCC against the selected SKU, and receive confirmation message that their email has been added to the notification list. | Accenture | ALL | Custom | Confirmed |  |\n| OM-034 | Inventory | The system will be able to send a back in stock email to customers on the list via SFCC, where the first x people on the list will receive an email once it is back in stock, where the value of x is configurable per regional site. The Notify Me queue follows a first-in-first-out basis. No loyalty tier prioritisation is applied to the notification queue. | Accenture | ALL | Custom | Confirmed |  |\n| OM-035 | Fulfilment & Delivery | The system will display both online and in-store purchase orders in the My Account Order History page, sourced from NewStore OMS via MuleSoft. | Accenture | ALL | Custom | Confirmed |  |\n| OM-036 | Order Creation & Processing | The system will include order data passed to MuleSoft, as noted in the existing Magento configurations (including but not limited to: product name, product category, product material/composition, and duties paid or flag (DDP or DDU)), to support generation of custom commercial invoices for international shipments and returns | Accenture | ALL | Custom | Confirmed | Additional Note: The Global-e connector stores 2 x transaction data in Magento, the B2B and B2C transaction data  @Tim Lavelle @Isabel Chaloner Do we know what this comment is about? |",
